<p><b>Thanitos's Bio:</b>
<table border=1 width=400>
  <tr><td>
  As I look back on these many months away from the only home I've ever known, I find myself taking frequent mental trips back to my childhood.  Only Innoruuk in his ultimate wisdom knows why.  Perhaps, if for no other reason,  then to contemplate the turn of events that have brought me to where I am today.  My upbringing in Calshinar Na'reysic or House Lo'radin, 6th house of Neriak, was not pleasant.  I was secondboy, and therefore looked down upon as nothing better than a servant, not a royal.  Dark elf men are considered a lower life form in Neriak anyway.  I never knew my father.  He was killed by my mother in a fit of rage one night shortly after my birth.  My mother is a very powerful cleric, as well as an evil one.  There were several stories that occasionally drifted through the servant's quarters where I lived.  I was not good enough to live in the main house with the rest of the family.  For most of my young life, I was under the care of my sister Traena, a disciple of Innoruuk and student of Nezka Tolax, the finest holy warrior in all of Neriak.  I followed her around hoping to learn from her but she cared not for the little waif who tagged along incessantly.  One day she was sent on a quest for decayed armor in a place called Casic-Thule.  I never saw her again, but her gnoll hide lariat left permanent reminders of our bitter and strained relationship.  Shortly after, I was taken under the care of my brother Taleran, firstboy of House Lo'radin.  He too was a Shadow Knight of great potential.  He trained me in the ways of the blade and taught me the essentials of efficient spell casting.  He schooled me in the ways of Innoruuk's meditation.  He taught me too well.  Taleran was not kind to me, however.  He beat me severely when I would make mistakes.  He nearly killed me several times and if it had not been for the house healer, I would surely have perished on more than one occasion.  I vowed revenge for his contemtable treatment of me.  Fortuneately, I was wise beyond my years.  I understood that the ambitions of my Matron Mother would not go unsated very long.  One day I heard of the plan to coup the 5th house of Neriak, House Zarishan.  My mother would not be denied her place in the circle of five, and soon the day for the attack came.  Her spies brought word of a fatal mistake by Matron Bernia and we struck.  It was a complete annhilation.  I used the chaos of our successful coup to exact revenge upon my brother and I slit his throat with an enchanted dagger as we made our way back from the celebration in Third Gate.  I had earned the right to take my place as first son of the new 5th house of Neriak, but instead I spit upon my brother's corpse and looted it of all it had.  I left House Lo'raden, never to return.  I made my way to the surface and began to acquire my fortune.  I occasionally stop into Neriak to deposit loot in the bank, or fill my pack up with rations, but I choose to make my way traveling across the lands of Norrath, spilling the blood of the weak and spreading the word of Innoruuk.  I have forsaken my family and taken the surname of Crimsonblade, appropriate because rarely is one able to see the true hue of my mithril weapon.  As I finish the entry into this journal, my heart pumps with the blood of a new purpose.  I have been accepted into an organization called the Bloodhorde.  They have the same goals as I do.  Eliminate good from the face of Norrath.  Slay in the name of all that is dark and sinister.  Kill, kill, kill.  My evil brothers and sisters have welcomed me and given me a new home and I take them as my family now.  Long live the Bloodhorde!_____________Thanitos Crimsonblade
  </td></tr>
</table>



